# Role-by-role usage scenarios

## Design Head
- Register a new idea with images and a concept note.
- Choose an automatic workflow pattern so the full task chain generates without manual entry.
- Reassign a task to a different employee without losing task history.
- See exactly why a design is blocked from release (missing approval level named explicitly).
- View team on-time rate and correction rate to coach effectively.

## Sketch Designer
- See only assigned tasks, sorted by due date.
- Start a task with the timer running server-side (survives a sleeping laptop).
- Put a task on hold with a reason while waiting for approval, without it counting against productivity.
- Upload a new sketch version when responding to a correction.

## Punching Designer
- Upload EMB/DST file with stitch count and machine format for downstream sample production.
- Get notified immediately when a correction is raised against punching work.

## Machine Operator
- Record machine details, output quantity and wastage for a sample run.
- Mark a task on hold when the machine isn't available, attributing the delay correctly.

## Sample Checker
- Run a quality checklist against a received sample; approve, reject, or request re-sample.
- Raise a correction with a clear type (mistake vs. machine issue) so responsibility is fair.

## Costing Team
- Enter time, material and machine cost; compare to the approved estimate.
- Be blocked from misusing cost entry to record employee mistakes (not their permission).

## Production Head
- See only fully approved designs with production instructions.
- Trace an issue back to the original design through cutting/embroidery/garmenting/finishing.

## Admin
- Manage process, sub-process, workflow pattern and hold-reason masters without a code change.
- Have every admin action audited automatically.

## Management / Owner
- Read-only view across all designs, corrections and KPIs.
- See design-success analytics by season, collection and product type.
